      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, that\u0027s because the BuildRequires are correct. However, if we ever install the -tests subpackage and try to run tests there (not during a package build), we will need those requirements to be present.\n\nIt\u0027s a bit counter-intuitive, but the rule of thumb for test requirements is:\n\n- They should be a BuildRequires, so the %check section can pass during the build.\n- And then, they should be Requires for the -tests package, so we can run them if we want when we install it using rpm.",
      "parentUuid": "ba7be1f8_68b4b8f2",
